# SUPERSEDED 2026-09-08 by pxqu-glm53flash-pxq2.tiers. Two reasons:
#   (1) the VRAM ledger in this header assumes GPU 0 still shares ~8.4 GB with another resident model;
#       it does not, so 4x P100 is 63.55 GiB and the fit is materially better.
#   (2) neither map names blk.45, which IS a full MoE block in the unsloth file --
#       under PXQU an unnamed expert stack lands on flat MXFP4. That is now refused by
#       the unmapped-expert guard in src/llama-quantize.cpp; kept here for the record.
# PXQU tier map 'pxqu-glm53flash-7card-resident': glm5next routed experts, blocks 3..44 x 3 tensors.
# expert budget 76.00 GiB -> 75.98 GiB used, avg 2.144 bpw, hist {'pxq1': 19, 'pxq2': 102, 'pxq3': 5}
# All seven cards (4x P100 + 2x V100 + 1080 Ti = 98.0 GiB), BOTH production seats down, experts fully VRAM-resident. Ledger: 98.0 - 6.21 overhead (7x280 ctx + 6x570 compute + 980 head) - 8.40 reserve (1.2/card) - 0.36 KV/state = 83.03 for weights; minus the 6.40 GiB backbone leaves 76.63 GiB of experts, budgeted at 76.00. Uniform pxq2 is 79.92 GiB and does NOT fit, which is why this map has a pxq1 floor.
# Shapes are the real ones from the unsloth UD-Q2_K_XL GGUF header.
# Solved by a Lagrangian knapsack on a PROXY sensitivity (depth x kind), not a
# measured sens.json -- no sensitivity sweep exists for glm5next yet. Regenerate
# from a real imatrix before treating the assignment as final.
# WARNING: this map places pxq1, whose wrel is an unmeasured proxy here.
# The precision-sensitive tensors (indexer.*, indexer_compressor_*, hc_*, ssm_a,
# ssm_dt.bias, ssm_f_*, ssm_g_*, ssm_norm, attn_k_b, attn_v_b, *_norm) are NOT in
# this map and must be left at source precision by the quantiser's keep list.
# Consumed by llama-quantize --pxq-universal.
^blk\.3\.ffn_gate_exps\.weight$=pxq1
^blk\.3\.ffn_up_exps\.weight$=pxq1
^blk\.3\.ffn_down_exps\.weight$=pxq2
